cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CATFLOW model container
message: >-
  A containerized gfortran build of the CATFLOW hydrological
  model, wrapped in a Python tool interface following the
  tool_spec Tool Specification.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ashish 
    family-names: Manoj J
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0625-7184'
  - given-names: CATFLOW
    family-names: Contributors
    affiliation: >-
      Original developers of the CATFLOW physically-based
      hydrological model
repository-code: 'https://github.com/CATFLOW'
url: 'https://github.com/CATFLOW'
abstract: >-
  CATFLOW is a physically-based hydrological model for simulating
  water flow and transport in hillslopes and catchments. The basic
  modeling unit is a 2-D hillslope, discretized by curvilinear
  orthogonal coordinates. Soil water dynamics are simulated based
  on the Richards equation; overland flow is simulated using the
  diffusion wave approximation of the Saint-Venant equation. This
  repository provides a containerized gfortran build of CATFLOW,
  wrapped in a Python tool interface that follows the tool_spec
  Tool Specification for reusable research software.
keywords:
  - docker
  - tool-spec
  - hydrology
  - catflow
  - hillslope
  - richards-equation
license: GPL-3.0
